[dbetz@magnus.ircc.ohio-state.edu (Drew Betz) writes:]
[] Yeah, I have to agree here.  Perhaps make choking a remote possibility
[] instead of a virtual certainty.  I would think overindulgence would
[] first result in upset stomach, then nausea, then vomiting.  Each of
[] these would be a decreasing probability.  Although its true people
[] can choke while eating, I would personally believe its more likely
[] when they are ravenously hungry and haven't eaten in awhile rather
[] than when they're gorging.

while eating is a required periodic necessity in the dungeon its
most useful purpose is to gain intrinsics.  it should then have
some attendant risks, so i don't think choking (to death) is out
of the question.  of course, you shouldn't choke unless:

1) the game has to tell you that you're full.
2) the game has to give you a clue that you're having a hard time eating.
3) the game has to give you an indication when it is safe to eat.
4) the game has to provide some means for you to preserve food.
5) the game has to provide some means for you to burn off calories.

without these then choking is unreasonable!!!  what? the game already
does these things?  nevermind ...

if you eat a really big meal despite the warnings then you deserve
to choke.  it's not like you have to eat the meal asap.

